Dear Students,

We are pleased to share the information about *Global South-Japan Tech
Talent Internship (GS-JTI)*, a program funded by Japan=E2=80=99s *Ministry =
of
Economy, Trade and Industry (METI)*.

The GS-JTI program offers students and recent graduates from eligible
countries the opportunity to take part in internships with Japanese
companies in advanced technology fields, including *IT, AI, and
semiconductors*. The program is designed to support practical skills
development, international exposure, and cross-cultural engagement through
real-world industry experience.

Through this internship, participants will have the opportunity to:

   - Gain hands-on experience with Japanese companies
   - Learn about Japanese workplace culture and business practices
   - Contribute to projects in technology-related fields
   - Build cross-cultural communication and professional skills
   - Explore potential future career opportunities in Japan



*Program Format*

The program offers both:

   - *On-site internships in Japan*: approximately *1.5 months*
between *September
   2026 and February 2027*
   - *Online internships*: approximately *1 month* during the same period

*Internship duration and format are subject to host company arrangements.*



*Eligibility*

Applicants must:

   - Be majoring in *STEM-related fields*, such as IT, AI, and
   semiconductors
   - Be *currently enrolled in a university* or have *graduated within the
   last three years*
   - Have *working proficiency in English*
   - Be a *citizen of a country listed on the OECD DAC List*
   *(excluding the People=E2=80=99s Republic of China)*
   - Be *residing outside Japan* at the time of application
   -

*Participant Support*

Support for the eligible participants includes:

   - Travel and accommodation assistance
   - Visa application support
   - 24/7 support during the internship period



Past participant feedback has also been positive, with program materials
indicating that *94% of interns expressed interest in working for Japanese
companies after completing the internship*.



*Program details:*
https://gs-jti.go.jp/foreign-talent/



*Registration and application:*
https://hub.techjapan.work/register



For any questions, please feel free to contact the program office via email
below.

